The coordinator sent a message while you were working:
Please recheck your judgement against the full POPL 2019 paper, which we now have. Pavol asked for this: "what if it contains important information that we should do something differently?"

The paper: "Polymorphic Symmetric Multiple Dispatch with Variance", Park, Hong, Steele, Ryu, PACMPL 3 (POPL 2019), Article 11. Full text: /home/user/fortress/research/decks/popl19w.txt (pdftotext -layout of research/decks/popl19w.pdf, 28 pages). Both files are gitignored; never commit either. Your judgement is explorations/reviews/decisions-review/judgement.md on main. When you wrote it, the record only had secondhand accounts of this paper, mainly explorations/reviews/mie-probes/literature.md.

Read the paper whole. Then go through every verdict of yours that the paper bears on. That includes at least:
- route A: the multiple-instantiation exclusion rule kept and the number tower flattened;
- answer 9 and the positional rule;
- the conversion-and-overloading decision of 2026-09-28;
- item 26, comprises read at the level of values, with its run-time uniqueness;
- item 30, a generic declaration beside a plain one;
- the implicit bound Any (R3);
- the covariant keyword (row 404);
- and the omissions you named.

For each one, say:
- whether the paper confirms it, contradicts it, or adds something the record lacks, citing page and section;
- whether anything should be done differently, and if so what, in which batch, and at what cost.

Don't restate the verdicts the paper leaves untouched; list them by name in one line. Measure nothing. This is reading and judgement only.

Main is closed to commits while batch 6.5b lands, so do not commit there. Create a worktree: git worktree add /home/user/fortress-popl-recheck -b wip/decisions-review-popl origin/main. Write explorations/reviews/decisions-review/popl-recheck.md there. Commit only that file, in one command, with the protocol's footer, and push the branch. End that file with a short section "For Pavol" in plain words: the question in one line, then what changes, if anything. Return to me the commit hash and that section.

Address this before completing your current task.

